# Round muse039: Muse Spark Open decode on bp, the card front's small launches run beside its two largest Q8_0
# reads.
# Decomposition: /Users/hckim/.cache/bloomery/placegen/muse039-decomp.md §1, §3, §4. Per layer the front runs
# ~40 latency-bound
# small launches (32 appends, q/k norms, rope, flash, norms) one at a time while ~85 % of the card's slots sit
# idle.
# F1 forks the chain from the per-head norms to the output norm (37 + 2 x sliding nodes, 57..83 us) beside the
# gate's
# gemv, copy and sigmoid (~114 us): the overlap is at least the gate's last wave (~54 us; an equal-priority
# grid's
# pending blocks dispatch first, rig-log 09-29) and at most the chain: -2.8..-4.5 ms. F2 forks the router
# (18..20 us)
# beside latent_down + its norm (~60 us): -0.4..-0.75 ms. Total -3.2..-5.2 ms of 60.7 = +5.6..+9.4 % at D=512;
# +5.1..+8.5 % at D=4096 (same ms off 66.4). Bit-identical: no kernel, launch or float order moves, only
# edges.
# Wall [derived]: 16 servers x (57 s load + 5 s) + 16 x 8 s decode + 8 x 43 s pp4096 = 22..26 min, builds
# before the lease.
kind: ab
question: does forking the attention chain and the router onto the step's Branch, beside the gate's and the
